        <owl:annotatedTarget>A general and temporary condition of partial or complete inundation of normally dry land areas from the overflow of inland and/or tidal waters, and/or the unusual and rapid accumulation or runoff of surface waters from any source. A great flow along a watercourse or a flow causing inundation of lands not normally covered by water.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GEMET: http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3301</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


